ord highs, 3 daily record lows","records":"Record highs and lows, by the decade that set them","change":"Youngstown's days and nights have warmed since 1986","rain":"Youngstown has gotten wetter"},"text":{"lede":"Yesterday's high of 41\u00b0F was typical for November 13.","t_yest":"November 13 was a typical day","p_yest":"The high of <strong>41\u00b0F</strong> was typical for November 13. The normal high for the date is 50\u00b0F, and the record is 71\u00b0F (1989). The low of <strong>33\u00b0F</strong> was typical for November 13.","t_rec":"Record highs and lows, by the decade that set them","p_rec":"If Youngstown's climate weren't changing, every year would have the same chance of holding a daily record. Since 2000, Youngstown has set <strong>59 standing record lows</strong>, fewer than the 100 that chance alone would give, and <strong>90 record highs</strong>, close to the 100 that chance alone would give. The 1930s hold the most record highs of any decade (108). Youngstown's all-time high is 103\u00b0F, on July 10, 1936.","t_chg":"Youngstown's days and nights have warmed since 1986","p_chg":"Across 96 complete years: Youngstown's average low shows no clear change: +0.01\u00b0F per decade, a range (\u22120.11 to +0.13) that includes zero. Youngstown's average high shows no clear change: +0.02\u00b0F per decade, a range (\u22120.11 to +0.15) that includes zero. July and August highs have edged down across the full record; the 1930s summers were the hottest in it. <strong>The last 40 years tell a different story:</strong> since 1986, lows have risen <strong class='sig'>+0.67\u00b0F per decade</strong> (95% range +0.31 to +1.03) and highs have risen <strong class='sig'>+0.61\u00b0F per decade</strong> (95% range +0.19 to +1.03). The full record joins different observing sites over the years, and a move (for example, from the city to a cooler airport) can hide or exaggerate a long-run trend, so the recent decades are the clearer guide here.","t_mon":"Lows rose in none. Highs rose in 1 of 12 months; 3 months fell.","t_rain":"Youngstown has gotten wetter","p_rain":"Youngstown's yearly precipitation has risen <strong class='sig'>+0.87 inches per decade</strong> (95% range +0.55 to +1.18), about +10.0 inches since 1910. The 1991\u20132020 normal is 41.2 inches a year. The wettest year was 2011 (54.01 in); the driest, 1963 (23.79 in).","show_snow":true,"sig_bars":{"lo":false,"hi":false},"t_year":"2026 so far: 5 daily record highs, 3 daily record lows"}}